\f1\b\fs24 \cf2 How to use:
\f0\b0 \cf0 \
\
Put this script in your iTunes Scripts folder. This is located in 
\f2\i \cf3 user name
\f0\i0  > Library > iTunes\cf0 . If there is no folder named "Scripts" there, create one and put the script in it. It will then appear in iTunes' Script menu, where you can activate it by clicking on its name.\
\pard\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\li180\ql\qnatural
\cf0 \
Select a Playlist, or select some tracks in a Playlist, and run "All Tag Data to File Comments". Choose to store Playlist names if you wish. The tags will be stored in the "Get Info" comment window of each file of the selected tracks.\
\
Later, run "Recover Tag Data from File Comments" on a selected playlist or some selected tracks. Any track whose file contains data created by the first script will have its tags re-assigned with the stored data. \
\
Additionally, if you have selected to store Playlist names, the tracks will be distributed to the appropriate Playlists, recreating them if necessary.\
\
\
\pard\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\li180\ql\qnatural

\f1\b \cf2 Issues:
\f0\b0 \cf0 \
\
\'a5 Perhaps this needs mentioning: \ul any current Comments in a file's Get Info will be obliterated.\ulnone \
\
\'a5 
\f1\b Smart Playlists
\f0\b0  are ignored.\
\
\'a5 Depending on how many tracks you have selected, \cf4 these scripts can take quite a while to run\cf0 . Neither script reports progress, as this just adds more "stuff" to do and steals processor time. Be patient. When the scripts are finished, you will be notified. If you receive any errors, let me know. My email is below.\
\
\'a5 "Recover Tag Data from File Comments" distributes tracks to their Playlists in the order that the tracks are encountered. The resulting Play Order will therefore probably be incorrect. If Playlist Play Order is important to you, consider using the 
\f1\b track number
\f0\b0  tags to establish a track order 
\f2\i before
\f0\i0  running "All Tag Data to File Comments". Later, after "Recover Tag Data from File Comments" has distributed the tracks, sort the Playlist by 
\f1\b track number
\f0\b0  and then use the Contextual Menu command "Copy To Play Order" to re-establish the correct Play Order.\
\
\
\pard\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\li180\ql\qnatural

